WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Start with the part you can observe.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Follow the relationship as it changes.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
Stiffness describes deformation under load; strength describes resistance to failure. They are different design questions.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
A flexible ruler and a brittle sample can differ in stiffness and failure behavior; do not infer one from the other.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Load-response graph

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
A material category is not a guarantee of strength, durability or safety. Processing and test conditions matter.

